{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":24585,"duration_api_ms":25527,"num_turns":8,"result":"I wrote the script at `src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`, but I haven't run it. My attempt to check the syntax with bpftrace needed approval, so it hasn't been parsed either.\n\nIt attaches to the `power:cpu_frequency` tracepoint and does three things:\n- **Live output:** it prints one line per frequency change, showing CPU, old MHz and new MHz.\n- **Summaries on Ctrl-C:** it prints the number of changes per CPU and the milliseconds each CPU spent at each frequency. It also prints a histogram of target frequencies.\n- **Last interval:** the time between a CPU's last change and Ctrl-C isn't counted in the residency figures.\n\nRun it with `sudo bpftrace src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`. The tracepoint only fires if your cpufreq driver reports transitions. `intel_pstate` in active mode usually doesn't, so you may see no output there.\n\nIf you'd rather it live somewhere else, or want a README to go with it, tell me.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5eb50bd1-7c93-4594-a354-2685e4cd28f1","total_cost_usd":0.0945037,"usage":{"input_tokens":16,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2502,"cache_read_input_tokens":182574,"output_tokens":1990,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2502},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":349,"cache_read_input_tokens":27580,"cache_creation_input_tokens":200,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":200,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":351,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000451,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":1990,"cache